WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.277
Identify, explain and apply the important ideas behind my first block program.

00:00:06.117 --> 00:00:11.797
Sprite: is a character or object in a block program. Block: is a drag-and-drop coding

00:00:11.797 --> 00:00:12.175
instruction.

00:00:13.033 --> 00:00:18.553
Stage: is where sprites perform actions. Event: starts a program when something

00:00:18.553 --> 00:00:20.393
happens. Loop: repeats instructions.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:26.192
Design a simple paper model explaining sprite, block and stage. Trade models with a

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:28.688
classmate and explain how your design works.
